{# Decision template: who carries the scene on when the player presses Continue Narration, as one choice over the
   legal (speaker, target) pairs the game enumerated. The player says nothing new and lets the scene play out:
   the person they are looking at speaks, otherwise the NPCs carry the conversation among themselves, and an
   outsider joins only when their interjection guidance matches. Rendered into a decisions request, never into
   chat messages. Sent when dialogue.decisions.useForSpeakerSelection is on; otherwise, or without a usable
   answer, the game falls back on the crosshair target, else whoever the last line was said to, else another
   participant, else the nearest NPC who did not just speak.

   Context set by the game: decision_pairs (key, speakerUUID, speakerName, targetKind, targetUUID, targetName),
   decision_speakers (UUID, name, distance, isVirtual, isPrivateVirtual), conversationParticipants (the UUIDs who
   said or were told one of the newest lines of dialogue), triggeringEvent (the continue request), crosshairTarget,
   lastSpeaker, lastDialogueTarget, events, maxRecentEvents. The virtual-NPC rules and no self-target are already
   applied to the pairs. Keys are short and numbered per request (s2_tplayer, s2_t5); use p.key as given. There is
   no none option: someone always speaks.

   A criterion is one line; profiles and other multi-line decorators belong in the state blocks. #}
{% set ss = get_speaker_selector_settings() %}
{% set tagCompanion = ss.tagCompanion %}
{% set tagEngaged = ss.tagEngaged %}
{% set tagInScene = ss.tagInScene %}
{% set lookedAtUUID = 0 %}
{% if crosshairTarget and crosshairTarget.UUID %}
{% set lookedAtUUID = crosshairTarget.UUID %}
{% endif %}

[ state last_exchange ]
{% if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") and existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "name") %}
{{ lastSpeaker.name }} spoke last, to {% if lastDialogueTarget.UUID == player.UUID %}{{ player.name }}{% else %}{{ lastDialogueTarget.name }}{% endif %}.
{% else if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") %}
{{ lastSpeaker.name }} spoke last, to no one in particular.
{% else %}
No one has spoken yet.
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ state recent_dialogue ]
{{ render_template("components\\event_history_compact") }}
[ end state ]

[ state location ]
{{ location }}
[ end state ]

[ state nearby ]
{% for c in decision_speakers %}
{% set cinfo = decnpc(c.UUID) %}
{{ cinfo.name }}{% if lookedAtUUID != 0 and c.UUID == lookedAtUUID %} [LOOKED AT]{% endif %}{% if exists("conversationParticipants") and c.UUID in conversationParticipants %} [IN CONVERSATION]{% endif %}{% if cinfo.isVirtual %}{% if c.isPrivateVirtual %} (virtual: a voice only {{ player.name }} hears){% else %} (virtual: heard by everyone here, but not physically present){% endif %}{% else %} ({{ cinfo.gender }} {{ cinfo.race }}, {{ units_to_meters(c.distance) }}m away){% endif %}{% if tagCompanion and is_follower(c.UUID) %} [COMPANION]{% endif %}{% if tagEngaged and is_in_package(c.UUID, "SkyrimNet_PlayerFollowPackage") %} [ENGAGED]{% endif %}{% if tagInScene and ((is_plugin_loaded("SexLab.esm") and is_in_faction(c.UUID, "SexLabAnimatingFaction")) or (is_plugin_loaded("OStim.esp") and is_in_faction(c.UUID, "OStimExcitementFaction"))) %} [IN SCENE]{% endif %}
- {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", c.UUID) }}
- Interjection: {{ render_character_profile("interject_inline", c.UUID) }}
{% endfor %}
Tags: [LOOKED AT] is the person {{ player.name }} is looking at. [IN CONVERSATION] said or was told one of the latest lines. {% if tagCompanion %}[COMPANION] travels with {{ player.name }}; that alone is no reason to speak. {% endif %}{% if tagEngaged %}[ENGAGED] is already in conversation with {{ player.name }}. {% endif %}{% if tagInScene %}[IN SCENE] is physically occupied in an intimate scene and speaks only if addressed by name. {% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ question next choice ]
Nothing new was said: {{ player.name }} is quietly letting the scene play out. Decide who speaks next and to whom. `recent_dialogue` is the conversation so far, oldest first; `last_exchange` says who spoke last and to whom.
When someone is marked [LOOKED AT], {{ player.name }} is looking at them: they speak next, to whoever the moment calls for.
Otherwise the people in the scene carry it among themselves. Someone the last line was said to, who has not answered, answers whoever said it. Failing that, another person marked [IN CONVERSATION] picks it up: they reply, react, disagree or take the topic somewhere new.
Anyone else, companions and virtual NPCs included, joins only when their Interjection guidance in `nearby` matches what was just said or what just happened. A match is specific: the general subject of the scene, being nearby, being a companion or having an opinion is not one. Someone whose guidance is missing or still a placeholder joins only when addressed. A virtual NPC has no body and needs a clear match.
The last speaker has just had their turn: choose them again only when no one else has a reason to speak.
Speakers address each other. Choose {{ player.name }} as the target only when the line is genuinely for {{ player.name }}, such as a reaction to something {{ player.name }} did; {{ player.name }} has chosen to listen.
When no conversation is under way, choose whoever has the clearest reason to speak in this situation.
[ criteria ]
{% for p in decision_pairs %}
{% set pv = false %}{% for s in decision_speakers %}{% if s.UUID == p.speakerUUID and s.isVirtual %}{% set pv = true %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{{ p.key }}: {{ p.speakerName }} speaks next, to {% if p.targetKind == "player" %}{{ player.name }}{% else %}{{ p.targetName }}{% endif %}{% if pv %} (right only if {{ p.speakerName }} was addressed or {{ p.speakerName }}'s Interjection guidance clearly matches what just happened){% endif %}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
